# Keep the build context to sources: `target/` alone is many GB and would be
# copied into the builder only to be ignored by cargo.
target/
# Not used by any build step — the Dockerfile is passed with -f. Excluding it
# means editing a compose file or the verify script does not invalidate COPY
# and trigger a full recompile.
deploy/
.claude/
.rift-ship/
.git/
vendor/rift/target/
vendor/rift/.git/
# The console bundle, its dependencies, and the wasm the bundle embeds are all
# produced by the image's own `wasm` and `web` stages (#265). Excluding them is
# what makes that guarantee real rather than aspirational: without it, a
# developer who has run `pnpm build` on the host gets that bundle copied into the
# builder by `COPY . .`, and the image's console is silently whatever was last
# built locally instead of what this Dockerfile produced. The stages COPY their
# own output in explicitly, so nothing here is lost.
web/dist/
web/node_modules/
web/public/lint/
# Vite inlines `VITE_*` values from a `.env` file into the bundle at build time,
# so a developer's local `web/.env.local` would otherwise be baked into a shipped
# image. There is no such file today; the exclusion is here so there never can be
# one by accident.
web/.env
web/.env.*
# Local test output. None of it can reach `dist/`, but all of it would bloat the
# layer and bust the `COPY web/ ./` cache after any local playwright run.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/dist-scan/
web/survey/
**/*.md
!README.md
